{% extends "_layout.html.j2" %}
{% import "_parts.html.j2" as t %}
{% set c = collections[0] %}
{% block content %}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px">Hello,</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 14px"><b>{{ c.title }}</b> is held in the CyVerse Data Store at
<code>{{ c.path }}</code> and is credited to {{ c.creator }}, with no individual named in its
metadata. We are moving the described community collections out of the legacy Data Commons into our
CKAN catalogue at <a href="https://dc.cyverse.org">dc.cyverse.org</a>, and this collection is one of
20 that qualify. Before anything happens I need to reach whoever is responsible for it. If that is
not you, I would be grateful for a forward or a name.</p>

{{ t.unchanged() }}
{{ t.mapping(c) }}
{{ t.arrives(c) }}

<p style="margin:0 0 8px"><b>What I need:</b></p>
<ol style="margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px">
<li style="margin:0 0 8px">Confirmation that you are the right contact, or a pointer to who is.</li>
<li style="margin:0 0 8px">Whether <code>{{ c.collection }}</code> should be in the catalogue at all.
This is opt-in: no reply means it is not published, and it stays exactly where it is today.</li>
{{ t.admins() }}
{{ t.licence(c) }}
</ol>

{{ t.handover(c) }}

<p style="margin:0 0 14px">The deadline is <b>{{ deadline }}</b>, with one reminder on
{{ reminder_date }}.</p>

{{ t.signature(sender_name, sender_title) }}
{% endblock %}
